308:/* A non-init thread's current connection: a pool lease (pooled=1) or, when the
309: * pool is exhausted/unavailable, a private overflow connection (pooled=0).
310: * Stored in g_thread_conn_key; the destructor returns/closes it on thread exit
311: * (this is the reliable reclaim-on-thread-death the pool reaper deliberately
312: * leaves to us). A failed acquisition never falls back to g_conn: libpq forbids
313: * concurrent use of one PGconn, and g_conn belongs exclusively to the init
314: * thread. g_lease_depth refcounts db2_lease_begin/_end so nested units
315: * reuse one lease. */
