575:       * key (the env then carries SSH_AUTH_SOCK + a TOFU GIT_SSH_COMMAND): honor
576:       * the SSH URL so key auth is actually used — the only way in for a host
577:       * that offers SSH-key access only (e.g. a corporate Bitbucket). Otherwise
578:       * clone over HTTPS: our default credential model is per-host HTTPS tokens
579:       * (+ OAuth), and normalizing ssh://, git@host:path, git:// to https lets a
580:       * public or token-authed repo still clone. */
