45:/* AIMEE_WEBCHAT_GIT=0 disables the whole webchat git surface — forge-token,
46: * clone, ops, per-host credentials, ssh-key, projects, session-dir, OAuth —
47: * without affecting the editor (which has its own AIMEE_WEBCHAT_EDITOR gate;
48: * session-dir is git-panel-only and not on the editor path, so gating it here is
49: * safe). On by default; only the exact value "0" disables it, so a blank/other
50: * value leaves git enabled. Read per call (immediate single-byte compare, like
51: * webuser_editor's AIMEE_WEBCHAT_EDITOR gate) — aimee never setenv()s at request
52: * time, so there is no concurrent-mutation window. Each git route checks this
53: * first and returns 503 when off — ahead of the 403 webuser check, which is
54: * intentional: the disabled state is not a secret, and an operator can ship the
55: * image with the editor but no git intake. */
56:int git_surface_enabled(void)
57:{
58:   const char *v = getenv("AIMEE_WEBCHAT_GIT");
59:   return !(v && v[0] == '0' && v[1] == '\0');
60:}
